      "content": "You are correct about APA 7th edition, I apologize for the mistake. The correct format for APA is to use \"et al.\" after the first author that is not part of a publication series that includes multiple authors, but if there are 3 or more authors in a single citation, \"et al.\" can be used starting from the beginning.\n\nAs for the Chicago style, here are the in-text citations:\n\n- APA 7th edition: (Smith et al.)\n- Chicago 17th edition (authors): (Smith)\n- Chicago 17th edition (editors/bibliographers): (Smith, Author)\n\nFor a source with multiple authors from the same publication series, APA would usually include the SES page numbers: (Smith et al., 2020, SES pp. 102-105) \n\nPlease note that APA style can be somewhat complex.",
